THE FAILURE THE DRY-RUN CANNOT CATCH, demonstrated:
  order=["not-a-real-provider"] with allow_fallbacks=false
    -> HTTP 404 "No endpoints found for deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731."
Note that message contains "no endpoints", so client.NO_ENDPOINTS_MARKER matches
it and the client treats it as RETRYABLE. A wrong slug would therefore not fail
fast: it would burn max_attempts=4 on every call and fail every cell slowly.
That is exactly why this check is run before the stage rather than after it.

